{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 29,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moreover, Job continued his parable, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh that I were as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " months past, as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the days ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "when",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God preserved me;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When his candle shined upon my head, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and when",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by his light I walked ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "through",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " darkness;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As I was in the days of my youth, when the secret of God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon my tabernacle;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the Almighty ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " yet with me, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "when",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my children ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " about me;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I washed my steps with butter, and the rock poured me out rivers of oil;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I went out to the gate through the city, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "when",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I prepared my seat in the street!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The young men saw me, and hid themselves: and the aged arose, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " stood up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The princes refrained talking, and laid ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hand on their mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The nobles held their peace, and their tongue cleaved to the roof of their mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the ear heard ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", then it blessed me; and when the eye saw ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", it gave witness to me:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because I delivered the poor that cried, and the fatherless, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him that had",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none to help him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The blessing of him that was ready to perish came upon me: and I caused the widow's heart to sing for joy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I put on righteousness, and it clothed me: my judgment ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as a robe and a diadem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I was eyes to the blind, and feet ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I to the lame.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a father to the poor: and the cause ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I knew not I searched out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I broke the jaws of the wicked, and plucked the spoil out of his teeth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then I said, I shall die in my nest, and I shall multiply ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " days as the sand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My root ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " spread out by the waters, and the dew lay all night upon my branch.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My glory ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fresh in me, and my bow was renewed in my hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " gave ear, and waited, and kept silence at my counsel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "After my words they spoke not again; and my speech dropped upon them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they waited for me as for the rain; and they opened their mouth wide ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for the latter rain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I laughed on them, they believed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not; and the light of my countenance they cast not down.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.29.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I chose out their way, and sat chief, and dwelt as a king in the army, as one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " comforteth the mourners.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
